5.1 Phase 1: Guardian Agent Core Infrastructure (2026–2027)

Focus: Establishment of core reference-based and reference-free evaluation flows, real-time guardrail execution, and automated EU AI Act documentation.

Milestones:

Q3 2026: Launch of the Critique Shadowing module, supporting expert-driven label collection and instant feedback synchronization.

Q4 2026: Implementation of the automated EU AI Act Technical File compiler (exporting certified JSON/PDF files matching Annex IV requirements).

Q1 2027: Deployment of real-time Guardrail Orchestrator with integrated, sub-500ms latency self-correction loops.

5.2 Phase 2: Multi-Modal & Agentic Verification (2027–2028)

Focus: Scaling evaluation architectures to audit physical systems, complex multi-turn multi-agent state machines, and multi-modal interactions (audio, image, code generation).

Milestones:

Q3 2027: Launch of Cross-Modal Consistency checking (verifying that generated audio/images correspond logically and safely with raw text traces).

Q1 2028: Implementation of Agentic State Machine auditing—actively mapping execution graphs to prevent loop traps, rogue tool invocation, and security escapes.

5.3 Phase 3: Autonomous Self-Healing & Closed-Loop Adaptation (2028–2030)

Focus: Completely autonomous quality platforms capable of self-correcting based on operational parameters and user feedback, requiring zero human engineering overhead for system drift remediation.

Milestones:

Q2 2029: Release of Self-Healing Agent Pipelines that dynamically rewrite system prompts and context-retrieval routing on the fly in response to detected instruction drift.

Q4 2029: Deep integration with hardware-agile compute routing, dynamically migrating validator instances across mixed GPU arrays (e.g., T4, A100, custom silicon) to balance operational cost, target accuracy, and strict latency SLAs.
